<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jubaland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Trans-Juba, Oltregiuba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jubaland is a region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jubba-river">Jubba River</a>, centred on the port of Kismayo. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> ceded it from Kenya Colony to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1924 as a reward for Italy's part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and it was joined to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a> in 1926. Since 2013 it has been an autonomous federal member state of Somalia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jubaland.jpg" alt="Jubaland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Derkommander0916 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jubaland_(Somalia).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
